IMPORT prelude

-- Work Health and Safety Act 2011 (ACT) -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- Built-in date functions only (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH, DATE_YEAR); no daydate.
-- "Within N months/years after a day": the period starts the next day (the day itself is excluded, as the Legislation
-- Act 2001 (ACT) s 151 is understood to say; that Act is not deposited) and ends on the same day of the month N months
-- (or years) on; where that month has no such day, on its last day (29 February -> 28 February). Fork F1 in NOTES.md.
--
-- (c) Australian Capital Territory. Used under CC BY 4.0 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md). Unofficial text.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Work Health and Safety Act 2011 (ACT)`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

-- Plain days from one day to another (negative if the second is earlier).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the start` `to` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

-- Whether the first day is strictly before the second.
GIVEN `the first` IS A DATE, `the second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first` `falls before` `the second` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second`

-- The later of two days.
GIVEN `the first` IS A DATE, `the second` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the later of` `the first` `and` `the second` MEANS
    IF `the first` `falls before` `the second` THEN `the second` ELSE `the first`

GIVEN y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a leap year` y IF
        ((y MODULO 4) EQUALS 0 AND (NOT ((y MODULO 100) EQUALS 0)))
    OR  (y MODULO 400) EQUALS 0

GIVEN m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last day of month` m y MEANS
    IF m EQUALS 2
    THEN IF `is a leap year` y THEN 29 ELSE 28
    ELSE IF m EQUALS 4 OR m EQUALS 6 OR m EQUALS 9 OR m EQUALS 11
         THEN 30
         ELSE 31

-- The day N months after a day: the same day of the month N months on, or that month's last day where it is shorter.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
n `months after` `the day` MEANS
    IF DATE_DAY `the day` AT MOST `the last day of month` `the month` `the year`
    THEN DATE_FROM_DMY (DATE_DAY `the day`) `the month` `the year`
    ELSE DATE_FROM_DMY (`the last day of month` `the month` `the year`) `the month` `the year`
    WHERE
        `the months counted` MEANS (DATE_YEAR `the day` TIMES 12) PLUS (DATE_MONTH `the day` MINUS 1) PLUS n
        `the year` MEANS FLOOR (`the months counted` DIVIDED BY 12)
        `the month` MEANS (`the months counted` MINUS (`the year` TIMES 12)) PLUS 1

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
n `years after` `the day` MEANS (n TIMES 12) `months after` `the day`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
n `days after` `the day` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the day` PLUS n)

